From be58f1e6bdc3405ea3ac7db86cbf2ba346bc0263 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:27:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 083/101] MAS local: shut Android down safely when Windows ends
 the session

Logging off, restarting or shutting down Windows stopped a windowed
instance as if the power were cut: Qt agrees to WM_QUERYENDSESSION at
once and quits on WM_ENDSESSION, with no guest sync and no Android
shutdown.

With the lean toolbar and a window (Windows only), handle both messages
in the native event filter before Qt does:

- WM_QUERYENDSESSION starts the same safe shutdown as the close button,
  with the windows left up, and refuses with a reason set through
  ShutdownBlockReasonCreate. Windows lists the emulator with that reason
  until the process has quit, and then goes on. A critical session end
  cannot be refused; it only starts the shutdown.
- WM_ENDSESSION with the session ending (shut down anyway, critical, or
  forced without asking) starts the shutdown if it has not started, or
  syncs once more if no sync is running (the first one may have failed,
  and Android may have written more since). It waits up to 3 s for the
  sync and then lets Qt quit, which stops QEMU.
- WM_ENDSESSION with the session going on hides the windows: Android is
  already powering off, and the instance carries on as after a close.

The process asks to be shut down before programs at the default level,
so that the private adb server is still there while the emulator
refuses and waits. The lean close path moves into
ToolWindow::beginLeanSafeShutdown, shared by both; it also closes the
extended controls, whose snapshot actions would race the shutdown while
the windows stay up. A repeated close during a shutdown with the
windows up hides them. Once a safe shutdown has ended, the window quits
Qt whether or not it was hidden.

The full toolbar (ANDROID_EMU_FULL_TOOLBAR=1) and the hidden-window mode
keep the upstream behaviour; headless instances are a separate change.
Still to be checked on a real logoff and restart: that Windows goes on
by itself once the refusing process has quit, how long it waits in
WM_ENDSESSION, and whether the reason shows once the windows are hidden.

